│  1 Do we need more context?                                        │
│    No. The necessary context has been gathered:                    │
│     • The use_required_attribute method in ClearableFileInput is   │
│       responsible for determining whether the required attribute   │
│       should be displayed.                                         │
│     • The logic returns False when initial is not None, preventing │
│       the required attribute from being displayed when a file is   │
│       already set.                                                 │
│  2 Bug locations and intended behavior:                            │
│     • Location 1:                                                  │
│       File: django/forms/widgets.py                                │
│       Class: ClearableFileInput                                    │
│       Method: use_required_attribute                               │
│       Intended behavior:                                           │
│       The method should return False when initial is not None,     │
│       ensuring the required attribute is not displayed when a file │
│       is already set. This aligns with the issue description.      │
│     • Location 2:                                                  │
│       File: django/forms/widgets.py                                │
│       Class: FileInput                                             │
│       Method: use_required_attribute (to be implemented)           │
│       Intended behavior:                                           │
│       The method should inherit the logic from ClearableFileInput  │
│       and ensure the required attribute is only set when no        │
│       initial data exists.                                         │
│     • Location 3:                                                  │
│       File: django/forms/widgets.py                                │
│       Class: FileInput                                             │
│       Method: value_from_datadict                                  │
│       Intended behavior:                                           │
│       This method should return files.get(name) when initial is    │
│       not None, ensuring the file input correctly handles initial  │
│       data.                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ Summary:                                                           │
│ The bug is in ClearableFileInput's use_required_attribute method,  │
│ which should be moved to FileInput to ensure the required          │
│ attribute is not displayed when initial data exists. The intended  │
│ behavior is to conditionally set the required attribute based on   │
│ whether initial data is present.                                   │
